+# Migrating a Nutshell mint to CDK
+
+`cdk-mintd migrate-nutshell` copies a Nutshell mint database into an empty CDK
+database of the same engine. It is an offline operation: stop the Nutshell mint
+and keep it stopped until cutover.
+
+This subcommand is not part of the stock v0.18.3 release. It is a port of the
+closed PR #2016, extended for Nutshell 0.20.3 through 0.22.x.
+
+## SQLite
+
+```bash
+cdk-mintd migrate-nutshell \
+  --source /path/to/nutshell/mint.sqlite3 \
+  --target /var/lib/cdk-mintd/cdk-mintd.sqlite \
+  --allow-empty-c
+```
+
+The target path must not exist. The migration writes a staging database and
+renames it only after verification succeeds.
+
+## PostgreSQL
+
+```bash
+cdk-mintd migrate-nutshell \
+  --source 'postgres://nutshell:password@127.0.0.1:5432/nutshell' \
+  --target 'postgres://cdk:password@127.0.0.1:5432/cdk_mint' \
+  --tls-mode disable \
+  --allow-empty-c
+```
+
+The target database must exist and be empty. The tool applies the CDK schema.
+
+## Options
+
+| Option | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `--source <path-or-url>` | Nutshell SQLite path or PostgreSQL URL |
+| `--target <path-or-url>` | Empty CDK SQLite path or PostgreSQL URL |
+| `--tls-mode <mode>` | PostgreSQL TLS mode for the target |
+| `--verify-only` | Verify an existing migration without writing |
+| `--allow-empty-c` | Replace an empty `C` on spent proofs with the generator |
+| `--allow-orphans` | Skip rows whose keyset is missing from `keysets` |
+| `--allow-unknown-schema` | Accept a schema outside 38-42 |
+
+## Verification
+
+The migration performs a verification pass before committing. Run it again
+without writing:
+
+```bash
+cdk-mintd migrate-nutshell --source ... --target ... --verify-only
+```
+
+## After migration
+
+Initialize the database-backed configuration with the original seed:
+
+```bash
+cdk-mintd --work-dir /var/lib/cdk-mintd config init --existing-mint --file config.toml
+cdk-mintd --work-dir /var/lib/cdk-mintd
+```
+
+CDK verifies the configured signer against the historical keysets. Preserve the
+original `MINT_MNEMONIC` as `[info].mnemonic` or the original
+`MINT_PRIVATE_KEY` / raw seed as `[info].seed`. Do not convert between them.
+
+On first start CDK rotates each unit's active keyset because Nutshell keysets use
+64 amounts and CDK uses 32. Old keysets remain valid for spending.
